2. alice_acp  (VENDORED under backend/vendor/alice_acp/)
================================================================================
Upstream source: V-SK/alice-acp  (sibling repo, internal)
Vendored commit: 61e1a59b540facec54a683aad58398e4ab4734e5  (branch prl-twpool)
Used as:         the Track-A inference engine. backend/ imports
                 `alice_acp.local_inference` (+ api_chat / api_chat_gateway /
                 mining_device glue). Installed as a normal path package via
                 backend/vendor/pyproject.toml (deps: SQLAlchemy + cryptography).
Why vendored:    so this (now public) repo is SELF-CONTAINED and CI can build the
                 Windows / Linux / macOS packages with NO access to the private
                 alice-acp repo. The whole pure-Python package is vendored (the
                 eager package __init__ chains transitively reach a handful of
                 sibling subpackages); only the inference path is exercised at
                 runtime. The native inference wheels (mlx / llama-cpp-python /
                 huggingface_hub) are imported LAZILY and ship via the per-OS
                 requirements, not this vendored tree.
Re-vendor:       copy src/alice_acp from the upstream repo at the desired commit
                 into backend/vendor/alice_acp/ (excluding tests/ + caches) and
                 update the "Vendored commit" line above.
License:         internal / first-party (same authorship as this repo).

